      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's basically what i was thinking but the problem is they've scrubbed so much of the early repo history that even if i show my work, they'll just claim i'm some talented dev who reverse-engineered it or something. it's like they've built this entire myth around these \"founders\" who are basically just actors for the VCs. if i wanted to show them that i didn't just understand the math, but that i actually pioneered the specific cryptographic primitives they're using, what kind of technical \"bread crumbs\" would be most effective to leave? like, something they couldn't argue was just a coincidence?",
